    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that Base16.decode() correctly accumulates output when fed data in arbitrary-sized chunks, including single bytes and chunks that split hex pairs. The hex string \"556E74696C206E6578742074696D6521\" decodes to \"Until next time!\". Each pair of hex characters represents one decoded byte: 55='U' 6E='n' 74='t' 69='i' 6C='l' 20=' ' 6E='n' 65='e' 78='x' 74='t' 20=' ' 74='t' 69='i' 6D='m' 65='e' 21='!'"
   },
